Cell["\<\
m sets photon indices -m through m; the photon-space dimension is 2 m + 1. \
modulation is a function of a dimensionless periodic angle with period 2 Pi.\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->295260243,ExpressionUUID->"c714d269-f7ad-7643-af26-53f00e664d15"],

Cell["\<\
For distinct sites, returns {FourierModulationMatrix, zeroMatrix}. For \
coincident sites, returns {identityMatrix, FourierModulationMatrix - omega \
DiagonalMatrix[Range[-m,m]]}. Coincidence uses a distance threshold of 1.*^-5.\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->471292905,ExpressionUUID->"87ebe0ce-5d1b-e947-b609-c346359c0121"],

Cell["\<\
The matrix entry with photon indices p and q uses the Fourier coefficient at \
q-p. The vector-potential forms use Exp[I amplitude \
(rf-ri).vectorPotential[angle]] on nonzero-length bonds; their onsite \
modulation is zero.\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->1573874334,ExpressionUUID->"7325a721-a8bd-4c4c-8975-6dc3964bd65c"],

Cell["\<\
The two-element vector-potential form assumes amplitude 1. Use PhotonDress to \
combine these factors with a bare hopping matrix.\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->1026566116,ExpressionUUID->"46ed9fb0-e4e5-e642-8811-90b54d9b20ce"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Fourier coefficients are computed by ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["NIntegrate"]], "paclet:ref/NIntegrate"},
   "RefLink",
   BaseStyle->{"InlineFormula"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Source Sans Pro",ExpressionUUID->
  "e73a70d2-92a0-9045-a20b-4196315ded94"],
 " with default AccuracyGoal -> 10 and Method -> \"LocalAdaptive\"; accepts \
",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["NIntegrate"]], "paclet:ref/NIntegrate"},
   "RefLink",
   BaseStyle->{"InlineFormula"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Source Sans Pro",ExpressionUUID->
  "66eefe48-0d39-a647-adb1-42a33ab5bd84"],
 " options."
}], "Notes",
 CellID->444140482,ExpressionUUID->"1509f1df-80c0-fc46-9e69-8a777866d278"]
}, Closed]],

